{
  "source": "Prompts/fake-trap-v13.mp4",
  "duration": 193.6,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.84,
      "text": "AI can fake a voice, a face, a video, or a screenshot, cheaply and convincingly."
    },
    {
      "start": 6.36,
      "end": 7.34,
      "text": "And it's only getting better."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.32,
      "end": 10.34,
      "text": "Knowing fakes exist isn't a skill."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.8,
      "end": 13.96,
      "text": "It doesn't tell you what to do in the 10 seconds after a clip hits your feed."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.72,
      "end": 18.2,
      "text": "A friend sends you a video of your principal announcing that school is closed next week."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.72,
      "end": 21.42,
      "text": "The face, the voice, and the hallway all look right."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.18,
      "end": 24.68,
      "text": "On the left, we see the mindset before AI."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.26,
      "end": 27.1,
      "text": "You study the pixels to determine the truth."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.1,
      "end": 30.58,
      "text": "Because it looks authentic, your call is, I'd believe it."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.36,
      "end": 32.18,
      "text": "Now look at the right side."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.8,
      "end": 36.0,
      "text": "In the AI era, you ignore the pixels and check the trail."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.72,
      "end": 40.46,
      "text": "You find no current closure notice on the school website, so your call is,"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.64,
      "end": 42.22,
      "text": "I'd wait for the school to confirm it."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.78,
      "end": 43.8,
      "text": "Appearance can mislead."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.4,
      "end": 45.78,
      "text": "The source trail can be checked."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.54,
      "end": 48.88,
      "text": "The fake trap is believing it because it looks real."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.56,
      "end": 53.9,
      "text": "There is an inverse trap as well, dismissing the actual truth because it could be a fake."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.9,
      "end": 57.5,
      "text": "A friend might fake a picture of your hockey buddies hoisting the Stanley Cup."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.1,
      "end": 59.16,
      "text": "Everyone knows it is fake."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.52,
      "end": 61.78,
      "text": "Everyone is in on the joke, and there is no harm done."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.78,
      "end": 64.56,
      "text": "Four reasons drive harmful fakes."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.34,
      "end": 66.18,
      "text": "First, money."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.0,
      "end": 68.96,
      "text": "Outrage gets clicks and ad revenue."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.72,
      "end": 70.56,
      "text": "Second, power."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.22,
      "end": 73.2,
      "text": "Changing beliefs changes how people vote."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.9,
      "end": 75.24,
      "text": "Third, fame."
    },
    {
      "start": 76.06,
      "end": 78.18,
      "text": "Viral clips bring followers, true or not."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.0,
      "end": 80.44,
      "text": "Finally, cruelty."
    },
    {
      "start": 81.3,
      "end": 83.7,
      "text": "Fakes made to humiliate, especially at school."
    },
    {
      "start": 85.34,
      "end": 89.92,
      "text": "Spiking emotions—outrage, fear, excitement, or hope—is your warning sign."
    },
    {
      "start": 90.64,
      "end": 93.66,
      "text": "A strong feeling is your cue to stop and run manual checks."
    },
    {
      "start": 94.5,
      "end": 97.56,
      "text": "If you try an AI detector, treat its verdict as a clue."
    },
    {
      "start": 98.06,
      "end": 98.66,
      "text": "Never a ruling."
    },
    {
      "start": 99.12,
      "end": 100.04,
      "text": "Those tools make mistakes."
    },
    {
      "start": 100.94,
      "end": 103.68,
      "text": "This board outlines a three-step framework for checking clips."
    },
    {
      "start": 104.28,
      "end": 105.14,
      "text": "First, the source."
    },
    {
      "start": 105.7,
      "end": 106.36,
      "text": "Who posted it?"
    },
    {
      "start": 106.6,
      "end": 108.44,
      "text": "And do they have a reason and way to know?"
    },
    {
      "start": 109.14,
      "end": 111.32,
      "text": "The next step is establishing context."
    },
    {
      "start": 111.32,
      "end": 114.08,
      "text": "You need to find out, when was this recorded?"
    },
    {
      "start": 114.5,
      "end": 117.02,
      "text": "What did the speaker say before and after this part?"
    },
    {
      "start": 118.0,
      "end": 118.94,
      "text": "Finally, corroboration."
    },
    {
      "start": 119.48,
      "end": 122.38,
      "text": "A claim requires an independent source to confirm the event."
    },
    {
      "start": 123.38,
      "end": 126.66,
      "text": "Apply these three checks back to the video of the principal closing the school."
    },
    {
      "start": 127.24,
      "end": 128.68,
      "text": "Think about how you would verify it."
    },
    {
      "start": 129.12,
      "end": 130.34,
      "text": "You go back to the source trail."
    },
    {
      "start": 130.98,
      "end": 134.44,
      "text": "Look for the full announcement on the school website and check which dates it covers."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.98,
      "end": 139.48,
      "text": "If the dates are unclear, ask the school office using the contact information you already have."
    },
    {
      "start": 139.48,
      "end": 143.96,
      "text": "Until the school confirms next week's closure, the claim is unverified."
    },
    {
      "start": 145.4,
      "end": 147.42,
      "text": "Verify somewhere the sender does not control."
    },
    {
      "start": 148.58,
      "end": 152.62,
      "text": "If someone posts a fake about you or makes an account pretending to be you,"
    },
    {
      "start": 152.88,
      "end": 153.88,
      "text": "tell an adult you trust."
    },
    {
      "start": 154.4,
      "end": 160.54,
      "text": "If it's safe, manually write down the username, the link, and the date so you can report it together."
    },
    {
      "start": 161.2,
      "end": 166.54,
      "text": "There is a strict rule for dealing with fake, nude, or sexually explicit images of anyone"
    },
    {
      "start": 166.54,
      "end": 167.08,
      "text": "under 18."
    },
    {
      "start": 167.8,
      "end": 168.9,
      "text": "Do not take a screenshot."
    },
    {
      "start": 168.9,
      "end": 172.78,
      "text": "Do not download it, and do not forward the image to anyone,"
    },
    {
      "start": 173.14,
      "end": 174.76,
      "text": "even if you are just trying to report it."
    },
    {
      "start": 175.38,
      "end": 180.24,
      "text": "Instead, ask a trusted adult to help you report the image directly through the platform's"
    },
    {
      "start": 180.24,
      "end": 181.18,
      "text": "built-in safety tools."
    },
    {
      "start": 181.72,
      "end": 185.06,
      "text": "NCMEX take it down, and CyberTipline can also help."
    },
    {
      "start": 185.8,
      "end": 187.66,
      "text": "Seeing or hearing isn't proof anymore."
    },
    {
      "start": 188.34,
      "end": 190.0,
      "text": "Check the source, not the pixels."
    }
  ],
